        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\alpha=65^\\circ$, $\\beta=25^\\circ$, $\\gamma=65^\\circ$.",
          "worked": "Using the angle sum in right triangle $ABM$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha&=180^\\circ-90^\\circ-25^\\circ\\\\\\alpha&=65^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nThe right angle at $B$ gives $\\beta=90^\\circ-65^\\circ=25^\\circ$. In triangle $ABC$, $\\gamma=180^\\circ-90^\\circ-25^\\circ=65^\\circ$.",
