              ]
            },
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{h}{a}=\\frac{b}{x+y}=\\frac{x}{b}$.",
              "worked": "Compare the side opposite $25^\\circ$ with the hypotenuse in each similar triangle. Since $AC=CM+MA=x+y$,\n$$\\frac{h}{a}=\\frac{BM}{AB}=\\frac{BC}{AC}=\\frac{CM}{BC}=\\frac{b}{x+y}=\\frac{x}{b}.$$",
